Disable WebRender feature selection on Solaris/SPARC.

The Solaris/SPARC WebRender/SWGL path still has unresolved big-endian
presentation issues that can fail during renderer startup or produce incorrect
output.  Disable WebRender at gfx feature-selection time on this platform so
Firefox uses the non-WebRender compositor path consistently.

Keep this as a Solaris/SPARC policy patch rather than a generic big-endian
change: it reflects the supported Userland runtime configuration, not an
upstream assumption that every big-endian target must disable WebRender.

Dependency: independent policy patch. It may be applied anywhere after the
source tree is unpacked, but is numbered with the rendering stack because it
selects the supported Solaris/SPARC runtime path.

--- firefox-153.0/gfx/config/gfxConfigManager.cpp
+++ firefox-153.0/gfx/config/gfxConfigManager.cpp
@@ -193,6 +193,15 @@ }
 
   ConfigureFromBlocklist(nsIGfxInfo::FEATURE_WEBRENDER, mFeatureWr);
 
+#if defined(XP_SOLARIS) && (defined(__sparc) || defined(__sparc__))
+  // WebRender backends are still not reliable on big-endian SPARC.
+  // Disable WR at feature selection time so GTK falls back cleanly to the
+  // non-WebRender compositor path instead of failing during renderer startup.
+  mFeatureWr->ForceDisable(FeatureStatus::Unavailable,
+                           "WebRender disabled on Solaris/SPARC",
+                           "FEATURE_FAILURE_WEBRENDER_SOLARIS_SPARC"_ns);
+#endif
+
   // HW_COMPOSITING being disabled implies interfacing with the GPU might break
   if (!mFeatureHwCompositing->IsEnabled()) {
     mFeatureWr->ForceDisable(FeatureStatus::UnavailableNoHwCompositing,
